 I will **pass**.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord has opened with a strong Full House (QQQ66). I do not have a Full House to beat it, as I lack any triplets. My only option to beat this hand is to use the Rocket (Red Joker + Black Joker). However, it is the very beginning of the game (Landlord has 15 cards left), and my remaining hand (singles and pairs with no straights or triplets) is structurally weak and cannot capitalize on gaining the lead. Wasting the Rocket on a mid-level hand this early without a plan to clear my hand is poor strategy. I should save the Rocket for a critical moment or to stop a more dangerous play later. I will rely on my teammate or wait for a better opportunity.\n\nReason: Using the Rocket on turn 1 against a Full House is inefficient given my remaining hand is poor (unconnected singles and pairs). Passing preserves the game\'s highest threat for a crucial moment.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
